/// Fn Module (Plan 390 §15.10)
///
/// Provides the `Fn` spec for closure types, mapping to Rust's `Fn` trait.
/// Auto only uses `Box` for Rust interop, so `Fn` is declared as an empty
/// spec (no methods — it's a marker trait). In a2r:
///   - `Fn` as a type annotation     → `Box<dyn Fn>`   (Type::Spec path)
///   - `Box<Fn>`                     → `Box<dyn Fn>`   (spec in container = dyn)
///   - `Box<Fn(A, B)>`               → `Box<dyn Fn(A, B) -> ()>`
///   - `Box<Fn(A) R>`                → `Box<dyn Fn(A) -> R>`
/// The `Fn(...)` signature form parses to Type::Fn (same AST as fn-pointer);
/// the transpiler renders it as `dyn Fn(...)` when it's a Box/Arc type arg.

/// Fn spec — closure trait (maps to Rust's `Fn`). No methods: the signature
/// is carried by the `Fn(...)` type-argument syntax.
spec Fn {
}
